{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor.signtwist_S4_fixed_is_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor.signtwist_S4_fixed_is_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringEllipticFactor.lean#L83-L93","doc":"Discriminator (integral form): a vector fixed by the **sign-twisted** action\n`(2,1,1,1) = std ⊗ sign` must satisfy `σ·v = -v` for the two transpositions\n`(1 2)` and `(1 3)`; over the coordinates this forces every entry to vanish, so\n`dim((2,1,1,1)^{S₄}) = 0` (genus 0). Encoded via the two transposition constraints:\n`(1 2)`: `b=-a, a=-b, c=-c, d=-d, e=-e`; `(1 3)`: `c=-a, b=-b, a=-c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor.std_S4_fixed_generator_in_std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor.std_S4_fixed_generator_in_std","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringEllipticFactor.lean#L78-L81","doc":"The generator `(1,1,1,1,-4)` of the fixed line lies in `std` (its coordinate\nsum is zero), so the `S₄`-fixed sublattice is nonzero — rank **exactly** one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor.std_S4_fixed_is_one_dimensional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringEllipticFactor.std_S4_fixed_is_one_dimensional","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BringEllipticFactor.lean#L66-L76","doc":"The `S₄`-fixed sublattice of the S₅ standard representation's integral form is\n**rank one** (`= dim_ℚ(std^{S₄}) = 1`): any vector fixed by the point-stabilizer\n`S₄` (equal first four coordinates, `a = b = c = d`) with zero coordinate-sum\n`a+b+c+d+e = 0` satisfies `e = -(4a)`, hence is the multiple `a · (1,1,1,1,-4)` of a\nsingle generator. This is the content of `genus(Bring/S₄) = 1` (elliptic),\ncorrecting a prior hand-computation that returned genus 0. ","signatureChunk":0}]}